{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01ZU:prose-0002", "parent_tag": "01ZU", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNotwithstanding the example above, for ``most'' finite sets of irreducible\nclosed subsets one can apply Lemma <REF_0001> above,\nat least if <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact. This is true because <MATH_0002> contains a dense\nopen which is separated.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-maximal-points-affine}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a57d66aac7e337d3e4f608245ba7db2b4c996e7c60d590d5ff4896dd3a0c32a", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:52b3e0d6551c765e77e673b49982beed23c08e05c0c51189c431dffdc6b023fc", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9651110046b3737a3aaba5f8ec6e85e5c672b54bb1c97d235ddf35facbbc4cf3"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:03J1:statement", "parent_tag": "01ZU", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact scheme.\nThere exists a dense open <MATH_0002> which is separated.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\subset X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-compact-dense-open-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:96bf45731bed5d3c5488bebdcea0ae248119212d95ba4746d60c6b26be62ea58", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4d699a35828cfe6c1fe50e4af34f00a490f6833487d73706809b3885fb93489e", "source_math_hash": "sha256:64da079f5c9651dde9615d8ba7ba5bfe7c85fff63adb6438489335c31b3d73f3"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:03J1:proof", "parent_tag": "01ZU", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Say <MATH_0001> is a union of <MATH_0002> affine open\nsubschemes. We will prove the lemma by induction on <MATH_0003>. It is trivial for\n<MATH_0004>. Let <MATH_0005> be a separated\ndense open subscheme, which exists by induction hypothesis. Consider\n<MATH_0006>\nIt is clear that <MATH_0007> is separated and a dense open subscheme of <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = \\bigcup_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} U_i$", "MATH_0002": "$n$", "MATH_0003": "$n$", "MATH_0004": "$n = 1$", "MATH_0005": "$V' \\subset \\bigcup_{i = 1, \\ldots, n - 1} U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nV = V' \\amalg (U_n \\setminus \\overline{V'}).\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$V$", "MATH_0008": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:969bc8a162656cdf48218ae72330a3c710b3b1660d07aece52b98e3d1502809f", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60401bef7dd43ea3a84705bcd275d87932368c9565a2edb3c97a7acd284bc82e", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7b2cc32c23e31366cdbdcd08677e8fbe357bf2f9a615d30382a6eed9873837c7"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01ZU:prose-0003", "parent_tag": "01ZU", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt turns out that, even if <MATH_0001> is quasi-separated as well as quasi-compact,\nthere does not exist a separated, quasi-compact dense open, see\nExamples, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nHere is a slight refinement of Lemma <REF_0002> above.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{examples-lemma-no-dense-separated-quasi-compact-open-in-qcqs}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-maximal-points-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:7cc784ee8789878e6ae429d3b0fe35c4f7b474045564806bfb6292fd575e2574", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:15bd97cd49fa005631addcd7d36271a5a528192783c89b24ae3dc0d4091ed508", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01ZX:statement", "parent_tag": "01ZU", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-separated scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be pairwise\ndistinct irreducible components of <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004> be their\ngeneric points. Let <MATH_0005> be arbitrary.\nThere exists an affine open <MATH_0006> containing\n<MATH_0007> and all the <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Z_1, \\ldots, Z_n$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\eta_i \\in Z_i$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\eta_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-point-and-maximal-points-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:1eabfd5e921a9bbcf146ec070099ffb2671c888df19029203159408338554952", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dfe0124f73aa85d0637d1f85ddb5caa86ef57bd3f2f04a0e0f9503d38cc53654", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a606fea0e13e71a985c9d688706a7b1946224690bd1be943dd70eb83fba3cfa2"}
